      "message": "There is one other use of `__attribute__((no_sanitize(\"cfi\")))` in SkVx.h and it is also wrapped in a `#if defined(__clang__)`.  That use is not using `SK_NO_SANITIZE` although it could in theory since it includes `SkUtils.h`, which includes `SkAttributes.h`.\n\nDoes it make sense to add a specific `SK_NO_SANITIZE_CFI` macro that incorporates the guard for clang?",
