      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T16:51:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that Skia compiles with `-Wno-attributes` (see `gn/skia/BUILD.gn`) to avoid this sort of issue, which is why this hasn\u0027t been picked up in local GCC builds.",
      "parentUuid": "e7c240b9_85787eff",
      "revId": "0d6eebd919ae3b9564f3d4094561410f680d9964",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f33f7975_b878b5e7",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T20:00:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "May be a larger issue, but it appears that Skia currently blanket adds\n\nC and C++\n-Wno-attributes\n-Wno-deprecated-declarations\n-Wno-maybe-uninitialized\n-Wno-psabi\n-Wno-switch-default\n-Wno-unused-parameter\n-Wno-unreachable-code\n\nC++ only\n-Wno-noexcept-type\n-Wno-dangling-reference\n\nSome of these may or may not still be needed, but in the case of `-Wno-attributes` this is due to the fact that while `__has_attribute` now exists so we can test if `no_sanitize` exists, because the warning is about the string inside we cannot test for support for that (arguably this attribute should have been split up into many `no_sanitize_foo` attributes so they could be individually detected).",
      "parentUuid": "dc1266e8_124263ab",
      "revId": "0d6eebd919ae3b9564f3d4094561410f680d9964",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
